Instruction: Read the segment of a merger agreement and answer the multiple-choice question by choosing the option that best characterizes the agreement.\nQuestion: Is “financial point of view” the sole consideration when determining whether an offer is superior?\nOption A: No\nOption B: Yes\n\nMerger Agreement: SECTION 8.3. Evaluation of Acquisition Proposals. <omitted> (f) Notwithstanding anything in this Agreement to the contrary, at any time before the Company Shareholder Approval is obtained, the Company Board may make a Company Recommendation Change or authorize the Company to terminate this Agreement under Section 10.1(c) if: (i) the Company receives a written Acquisition Proposal that was not solicited in violation of this Section 8.3; (ii) the Company Board determines in good faith, after consultation with its financial advisor of national standing and outside legal counsel, that such Acquisition Proposal constitutes a Superior Proposal and that the failure to make a Company Recommendation Change or terminate this Agreement under Section 10.1(c) would be inconsistent with the Company Board’s fiduciary duties under applicable law; (iii) the Company Board provides Parent with at least five Business Days’ prior written notice of its intention to make a Company Recommendation Change or terminate this Agreement, which notice shall include the identity of the party making such Acquisition Proposal, a copy of the proposed definitive agreement, and a summary of the material terms and conditions of such Acquisition Proposal; (iv) during the five Business Day period following the delivery of the notice referred to in clause (iii), the Company Board and its advisors shall negotiate in good faith with Parent should Parent propose to make amendments to the terms and conditions of this Agreement such that the Acquisition Proposal would no longer constitute a Superior Proposal; and (v) after taking into account any amendments to this Agreement proposed by Parent in writing and after consultation with its financial advisor and outside legal counsel, the Company Board shall have determined in good faith that such Acquisition Proposal continues to be a Superior Proposal and that the failure to make a Company Recommendation Change or terminate this Agreement under Section 10.1(c) would still be inconsistent with the Company Board’s fiduciary duties under applicable law. (Pages 85-86)\nAnswer:
