Instruction: Read the segment of a merger agreement and answer the multiple-choice question by choosing the option that best characterizes the agreement.\nQuestion: Is \u201cfinancial point of view\u201d the sole consideration when determining whether an offer is superior?\nOption A: No\nOption B: Yes\n\nMerger Agreement: SECTION 8.3. Evaluation of Acquisition Proposals. <omitted> (f) Notwithstanding any provision in this Agreement, the Company Board may only consider an Acquisition Proposal if the following conditions are met: (i) the Company Board, after consulting with its outside legal counsel, determines in good faith that the proposal complies with applicable legal obligations, (ii) the Company Board, after consulting with its strategic advisors, determines that the proposal aligns with the long-term strategic goals of the Company, and (iii) the Company Board, after consulting with a financial advisor of a nationally recognized reputation, determines that the financial terms of the proposal are superior. If any of these conditions are not met, the proposal shall not be considered superior. (Pages 88-89)\nAnswer:
Choices:
